From 7f90e373a010af8ec30795533c506bb3e9b458d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:04:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): record why the dispatcher passed over a
 ready card; name it in ready-wait notices

Defect kanban-dd62aef001 (hub, 2026-11-10): t_01a1c7a0c8139180 (bb-tuner, pinned claude-opus-5-5/anthropic)
sat ready 33 min with free slots and no claimed/skipped_*/respawn_guarded event. The chat-wait and
parent-unclaimed notices said "1 card(s) ahead of it, 4/7 worker slots busy" and advised a priority bump,
which did nothing; the tick logs had rotated, so the skip site was lost.

- New hermes_cli/kanban_dispatch_skip.py. record_tick (run from the observe_dispatch post-result seam,
  non-dry ticks only) appends ONE `dispatch_skipped {reason, detail, until?}` event per card, reason and
  ready episode for skipped_ineligible, capsule_refused, no_progress_held, per_profile_capped,
  claim_deferred (Board/claim refusals), owner_down and pinned_quota_wall. A repeated reason adds nothing;
  a changed reason appends; at most 16 per episode.
- Lane admission holds a fresh card (no run yet) on the ready lane whose explicit concrete pin is
  live-quota-walled (kanban_provider_walls.live_quota_wall): resolve_dispatch_tier routes such a card
  straight to its pin, so a claim only spawned a worker into the wall. Reason pinned_quota_wall,
  until = the reset; clock_held so the stuck warning names the deadline.
- kanban_queue_position (local lane: `skip`), describe, kanban_parent_unclaimed _queue_words / notice_text
  / ready_hint and kanban_chat_wait.notice_text name the latest skip of the ready episode plus its until
  ("held: pinned model claude-opus-5-5 (anthropic) quota-walled until 10:00Z") and drop the priority
  advice unless the skip is about ordering (claim_deferred capacity). A local card ready >= 30 min with
  free slots and no recorded reason reads "dispatcher skip reason unrecorded", without priority advice.
- Latest-event readers that dedupe their own audit rows (note_nonspawnable, note_unplaceable, capsule
  refusal, goal_run_status changes_requested, guard-hold runs, the stranded diagnostic's hold reason)
  ignore dispatch_skipped, so the new rows neither restart a guard hold nor re-trigger those writers.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dispatch_skip.py (15 tests). On origin/main with only the new module
present, 7 fail, including the incident shape (the walled fresh pin is spawned, no event). With the fix all
pass; 168 test files importing the touched modules (kanban dispatch/notice/queue/walls/quota suites) pass
after updating test_kanban_provider_walls' fresh walled exact pin, which is now held instead of spawned.
